{
  "raw": {
    "https://www.northwestu.edu/jobs/faculty/assistant-or-associate-professor-of-graduate-counseling-12-month-position": {
      "title": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Graduate Counseling (12 month position)",
      "description": "Assistant or Associate Professor of Graduate Counseling (12 month position) | Northwest University Skip Navigation Menu Close Visit Apply Request Info Give Search Search Admissions + Campus Admission (Undergrad) Online Admission Graduate Admission Northwest Partnership Program International Students College in High School Re-admit or Change Campus Campus Visits and Info Sessions Academics + College of Arts, Sciences, and Technology College of Ministry College of Social and Behavioral Sciences School of Business School of Education School of Nursing School of PA Medicine Center for Leadership Studies Creatio Center for Technology, Media, and Design Faculty Directory Financial Aid + Scholarships Undergraduate Graduate Online Undergraduate Online Graduate Northwest Partnership Program Veterans/Tuition Assistance Glossary of Terms Cost Information Campus Life + NU Calendar Campus Tour Campus Ministries Eagle Store NU Library Student Housing NU Blog About + Mission, Vision, Values Office of the President Upcoming Events Student Consumer Information Student Success Conference and Event Services Job Opportunities Nondiscrimination & Title IX Contact Us Athletics Links For New Students Current Students Parents & Families Alumni Donors Veterans Home Jobs Current Job Opportunities at Northwest Apply Now About NU Explore this Section Job Opportunities On-Campus Student Jobs Part-Time Off Campus Assistant or Associate Professor of Graduate Counseling (12 month position) Position Details Department College of Social and Behavioral Sciences Reports To Dean, College of Social and Behavioral Sciences Appointment Fall 2026 Close Date Open Until Filled Classification Faculty, Full-Time (Tenure Track) Position Summary Northwest University is seeking a full-time (12-month), tenure-track faculty member within the College of Social and Behavioral Sciences. This assistant/associate professor position focuses   on teaching graduate counseling courses (on-campus and online) primarily in Northwest University’s Master of Arts in Clinical Mental Health (CMHC) Program, supporting students in their development as counselors, helping to maintain the program’s CACREP accreditation and participating in the life of the university through committee and other service work. Faculty members have the opportunity to become members of a vibrant Christian community, that is dedicated to spiritual vitality, academic excellence and empowered engagement with human need. Faculty members are also expected to fully participate in university life including committee work and other institution activities. Faculty: full-time tenure track position.  Contract renewal contingent on performance. There are 2 open positions in our CMHC program. Qualifications Has an earned Ph.D., Ed.D., or candidacy status in Counseling Education preferably from a CACREP accredited program; Possesses a deep, personal commitment to Jesus Christ, a Spirit-filled life, and demonstrates integration of faith and learning; Is licensed as a LMHC in Washington State (or is license eligible in Washington State). Has had successful teaching experience at the university level; Has knowledge about state licensure standards for LMHC (preferred); Is knowledgeable about CACREP standards (preferred). Is committed to establishing and maintaining positive mentoring relationships with a diverse student body; Is committed to establishing and maintaining positive relationships with faculty, staff, and the general constituency of Northwest University; Is committed to intercultural education and multicultural counseling and is committed to integrating faith into the counseling curriculum; Is committed to the development of skills in his/her students by coaching, modeling, and direct instruction; Has commitment to the values of NU and the CSBS vision; Demonstrates commitment to maintaining a safe work environment free of harassment, violence, and unlawful discrimination; Communicates effectively, gets along well with co-workers, and deals effectively and professionally with colleagues; and Has a clear counseling identity as evidenced by memberships in professional counseling organizations; professional counseling credentials and sustained professional engagement. Compensation Dependent on education and experience and based upon the established faculty salary schedule starting at the respective professor rank. ($81,463-$91,735) Application Requirements To be considered as a candidate, the applicant must submit the following documents and information: Letter of interest Curriculum vitae (including courses taught) Three professional references with contact information Documentation of current state licensure Statement describing how Christian faith shapes the candidate’s approach to counseling psychology Brief narrative of personal faith journey and current church involvement Search procedures will be closed when a sufficient number of qualified applicants have been identified. Contact Information Robert Campbell, Dean of CSBS .(JavaScript must be enabled to view this email address) Search procedures will be closed, when a sufficient number of qualified applicants have been identified. Applicants are urged to provide sufficient information, so that the application file may be considered complete at the end of the search period. Northwest University Northwest University is a Christian coeducational undergraduate and graduate institution, related to the Assemblies of God, offering baccalaureate and master's, and doctoral level education. The sixty-acre campus is located in Kirkland, Washington, just ten miles from downtown Seattle. The campus is an ideal setting for study, recreation, and inspiration and is centrally located and convenient to industry, business, and commercial activities. Mission Statement We, the people of Northwest University, carry the call of God by continually building a learning community dedicated to spiritual vitality, academic excellence, and empowered engagement with human need. In addition, all faculty members at Northwest University must subscribe to our Statement of Faith . Accreditation Northwest University is accredited by the Northwest Commission on Colleges and Universities (regional). The University is endorsed by the Commission on Christian Higher Education of the Assemblies of God and the Association of Christian Schools International. The University holds membership in the Council of Christian Colleges and Universities . Northwest University's College of Business is accredited by the Accreditation Council for Business Schools and Programs (ACBSP) . The Buntain College of Nursing’s baccalaureate degree is accredited by the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education . In addition, the College of Nursing has received approval from the Washington State Nursing Care Quality Assurance Commission . The University is also approved by the Board of Education and Superintendent of Public Instruction of the State of Washington to prepare elementary and secondary education teachers and recommend for certification. It is a member of the American Association of Colleges for Teacher Education. Northwest University's doctoral program in counseling psychology is accredited by the American Psychological Association (APA) . The University is approved by the Federal and State Governments for student aid programs and for the training of international students. Selected programs of study are approved by a Washington State Approving Agency for enrollment of those eligible for benefits under Title 38 and Title 10, U.S. Code and by Washington State for training in Vocational Rehabilitation. It is listed in the current bulletin, \"Accredited Higher Education Institutions,\" published by the U.S. Office of Education. Back to Job Opportunities How Can We Best Serve You? Find Your Major Schedule a Visit Apply Today Address 5520 108th Ave. N.E. Kirkland, WA 98033 Directions Contact 425-822-8266 info@northwestu.edu Campus Map Connect NU Calendar Employment Consumer Information Title IX Emergency Accreditation Finances Social Media Policy Privacy Policy Pay My Bill Northwest University admits students of any race, color, national and ethnic origin to all the rights, privileges, programs, and activities generally afforded or made available to students at the university. Northwest does not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, national and ethnic origin, age, disability, or status as a veteran in the administration of its educational policies, admissions policies, or scholarship and loan programs and athletic and other school-administered programs. © Copyright 2026"
    },
    "https://www.northwestu.edu/jobs/faculty/master-in-teaching-field-supervisor": {
      "title": "Master in Teaching Field Supervisor",
      "description": "Master in Teaching Field Supervisor | Northwest University Skip Navigation Menu Close Visit Apply Request Info Give Search Search Admissions + Campus Admission (Undergrad) Online Admission Graduate Admission Northwest Partnership Program International Students College in High School Re-admit or Change Campus Campus Visits and Info Sessions Academics + College of Arts, Sciences, and Technology College of Ministry College of Social and Behavioral Sciences School of Business School of Education School of Nursing School of PA Medicine Center for Leadership Studies Creatio Center for Technology, Media, and Design Faculty Directory Financial Aid + Scholarships Undergraduate Graduate Online Undergraduate Online Graduate Northwest Partnership Program Veterans/Tuition Assistance Glossary of Terms Cost Information Campus Life + NU Calendar Campus Tour Campus Ministries Eagle Store NU Library Student Housing NU Blog About + Mission, Vision, Values Office of the President Upcoming Events Student Consumer Information Student Success Conference and Event Services Job Opportunities Nondiscrimination & Title IX Contact Us Athletics Links For New Students Current Students Parents & Families Alumni Donors Veterans Home Jobs Current Job Opportunities at Northwest Apply Now About NU Explore this Section Job Opportunities On-Campus Student Jobs Part-Time Off Campus Master in Teaching Field Supervisor Position Details Department College of Professional Studies, School of Education Reports To MIT Program Lead Appointment January - June Close Date Open Until Filled Classification Adjunct, part-time Position Summary The School of Education at Northwest University invites applications for part-time Master in Teaching (MIT) Field Supervisors to support graduate teacher candidates during their student teaching experiences from January through June. Field Supervisors serve as mentors, coaches, and university representatives as candidates transition from coursework into classroom practice. Supervisors observe candidates in their K–12 placements, provide constructive feedback, collaborate with mentor teachers, and support candidates’ growth in effective, culturally responsive teaching. This is a flexible adjunct position. Field Supervisors may supervise two to ten candidates, depending on interest and availability. Supervisors are consulted regarding the location of each placement before assignments are finalized. Ideal candidates are experienced educators who enjoy mentoring emerging teachers and can provide both encouragement and thoughtful, actionable feedback. Candidates must be able to affirm and support Northwest University’s Statement of Faith and mission as a Christian university. Application review will begin immediately and continue until the School of Education’s supervision needs have been met. Essential Functions Mentor and support assigned MIT teacher candidates throughout part-time and full-time student teaching. Conduct at least four in-person observations of each assigned candidate and provide timely written and verbal feedback. Coach candidates in instructional planning, classroom management, assessment, differentiation, culturally responsive teaching, and reflective practice. Maintain regular communication with candidates and mentor teachers and collaborate to support a successful field experience. Complete required candidate evaluations and program documentation by established deadlines. Communicate concerns promptly to the MIT Program Lead and assist with problem-solving when challenges arise. Serve as a professional liaison between Northwest University and partner K–12 schools. Qualifications Required: Master’s degree in education or a related field. Current or previous state teaching certification. Significant successful K–12 teaching experience. Strong communication and interpersonal skills. Ability to provide constructive, growth-oriented feedback to developing teachers. Alignment with Northwest University’s mission and Statement of Faith. Preferred: Experience mentoring, coaching, or supervising teachers or student teachers. Familiarity with Washington State teacher certification expectations and the InTASC teaching standards. Compensation Field Supervisors are compensated $931.20 per teaching candidate supervised. Mileage for required travel to assigned school sites is reimbursed according to Northwest University policy. Application Requirements Interested candidates should submit: A current résumé or curriculum vitae. A brief cover letter describing relevant K–12 teaching, mentoring, coaching, or supervisory experience. Contact information for two professional references. A brief statement describing alignment with Northwest University’s Christian mission and Statement of Faith. Additional documentation may be requested prior to appointment.  Applications will be reviewed as received and positions will remain open until supervision needs have been met. Contact Information Heather Lucas, Assistant Dean .(JavaScript must be enabled to view this email address) Search procedures will be closed, when a sufficient number of qualified applicants have been identified. Applicants are urged to provide sufficient information, so that the application file may be considered complete at the end of the search period. Northwest University Northwest University is a Christian coeducational undergraduate and graduate institution, related to the Assemblies of God, offering baccalaureate and master's, and doctoral level education. The sixty-acre campus is located in Kirkland, Washington, just ten miles from downtown Seattle. The campus is an ideal setting for study, recreation, and inspiration and is centrally located and convenient to industry, business, and commercial activities. Mission Statement We, the people of Northwest University, carry the call of God by continually building a learning community dedicated to spiritual vitality, academic excellence, and empowered engagement with human need. In addition, all faculty members at Northwest University must subscribe to our Statement of Faith . Accreditation Northwest University is accredited by the Northwest Commission on Colleges and Universities (regional). The University is endorsed by the Commission on Christian Higher Education of the Assemblies of God and the Association of Christian Schools International. The University holds membership in the Council of Christian Colleges and Universities . Northwest University's College of Business is accredited by the Accreditation Council for Business Schools and Programs (ACBSP) . The Buntain College of Nursing’s baccalaureate degree is accredited by the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education . In addition, the College of Nursing has received approval from the Washington State Nursing Care Quality Assurance Commission . The University is also approved by the Board of Education and Superintendent of Public Instruction of the State of Washington to prepare elementary and secondary education teachers and recommend for certification. It is a member of the American Association of Colleges for Teacher Education. Northwest University's doctoral program in counseling psychology is accredited by the American Psychological Association (APA) . The University is approved by the Federal and State Governments for student aid programs and for the training of international students. Selected programs of study are approved by a Washington State Approving Agency for enrollment of those eligible for benefits under Title 38 and Title 10, U.S. Code and by Washington State for training in Vocational Rehabilitation. It is listed in the current bulletin, \"Accredited Higher Education Institutions,\" published by the U.S. Office of Education. Back to Job Opportunities How Can We Best Serve You? Find Your Major Schedule a Visit Apply Today Address 5520 108th Ave. N.E. Kirkland, WA 98033 Directions Contact 425-822-8266 info@northwestu.edu Campus Map Connect NU Calendar Employment Consumer Information Title IX Emergency Accreditation Finances Social Media Policy Privacy Policy Pay My Bill Northwest University admits students of any race, color, national and ethnic origin to all the rights, privileges, programs, and activities generally afforded or made available to students at the university. Northwest does not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, national and ethnic origin, age, disability, or status as a veteran in the administration of its educational policies, admissions policies, or scholarship and loan programs and athletic and other school-administered programs. © Copyright 2026"
    },
    "https://www.northwestu.edu/jobs/faculty/adjunct-pa-educator-in-clinical-medicine-multiple-openings": {
      "title": "Position Summary",
      "description": "Adjunct PA Educator in Clinical Medicine (multiple openings) | Northwest University Skip Navigation Menu Close Visit Apply Request Info Give Search Search Admissions + Campus Admission (Undergrad) Online Admission Graduate Admission Northwest Partnership Program International Students College in High School Re-admit or Change Campus Campus Visits and Info Sessions Academics + College of Arts, Sciences, and Technology College of Ministry College of Social and Behavioral Sciences School of Business School of Education School of Nursing School of PA Medicine Center for Leadership Studies Creatio Center for Technology, Media, and Design Faculty Directory Financial Aid + Scholarships Undergraduate Graduate Online Undergraduate Online Graduate Northwest Partnership Program Veterans/Tuition Assistance Glossary of Terms Cost Information Campus Life + NU Calendar Campus Tour Campus Ministries Eagle Store NU Library Student Housing NU Blog About + Mission, Vision, Values Office of the President Upcoming Events Student Consumer Information Student Success Conference and Event Services Job Opportunities Nondiscrimination & Title IX Contact Us Athletics Links For New Students Current Students Parents & Families Alumni Donors Veterans Home Jobs Current Job Opportunities at Northwest Apply Now About NU Explore this Section Job Opportunities On-Campus Student Jobs Part-Time Off Campus Adjunct PA Educator in Clinical Medicine (multiple openings) Position Details Department School of PA Medicine Reports To Dean, School of Physician Assistant Medicine Appointment Continuous Recruitment Close Date Open Until Filled Classification Adjunct, Part-Time Position Summary The School of PA Medicine currently seeks adjuncts in the following modules: Behavioral Health, Emergency Medicine, Genitourinary, Pediatrics, Surgery Essential Functions Instruct in the Clinical Medicine Course Series (a modular course series) according to area of expertise. Prepare presentations and course curriculum including assisting in creating exam questions for material covered. Assist Course Director in remediation plans for students as needed. Qualifications The successful candidate: Holds appropriate degrees from accredited colleges or universities: Masters degree or higher. Holds a current unrestricted license to practice as a PA or physician in the State of Washington. Has current clinical experience of at least two years in the clinical subject area being taught. Possesses a deep, personal commitment to Jesus Christ and to the Spirit-filled life. Demonstrates a commitment to the integration of faith and learning. Indicates a commitment to helping students to achieve PA program learning outcomes and objectives specific to the courses taught. Establishes and maintains positive relationships with students, faculty, university staff, and the general constituency of the University. Continually develops professional skills in aspiring students through coaching, modeling, evaluation, feedback, and direct instruction. Compensation The compensation per course credit hour is $1850. Application Requirements To be considered as a candidate, the applicant must submit the following documents and information: Letter of interest Curriculum vitae Names, addresses, email addresses, and telephone numbers of at least three references Brief statement of personal faith journey and church involvements Please email your documents to: Heather Deibler PA-C Dean of the Northwest University School of PA Medicine heather.deibler@northwestu.edu Search procedures will be closed, when a sufficient number of qualified applicants have been identified. Applicants are urged to provide sufficient information, so that the application file may be considered complete at the end of the search period. Search procedures will be closed, when a sufficient number of qualified applicants have been identified. Applicants are urged to provide sufficient information, so that the application file may be considered complete at the end of the search period. Northwest University Northwest University is a Christian coeducational undergraduate and graduate institution, related to the Assemblies of God, offering baccalaureate and master's, and doctoral level education. The sixty-acre campus is located in Kirkland, Washington, just ten miles from downtown Seattle. The campus is an ideal setting for study, recreation, and inspiration and is centrally located and convenient to industry, business, and commercial activities. Mission Statement We, the people of Northwest University, carry the call of God by continually building a learning community dedicated to spiritual vitality, academic excellence, and empowered engagement with human need. In addition, all faculty members at Northwest University must subscribe to our Statement of Faith . Accreditation Northwest University is accredited by the Northwest Commission on Colleges and Universities (regional). The University is endorsed by the Commission on Christian Higher Education of the Assemblies of God and the Association of Christian Schools International. The University holds membership in the Council of Christian Colleges and Universities . Northwest University's College of Business is accredited by the Accreditation Council for Business Schools and Programs (ACBSP) . The Buntain College of Nursing’s baccalaureate degree is accredited by the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education . In addition, the College of Nursing has received approval from the Washington State Nursing Care Quality Assurance Commission . The University is also approved by the Board of Education and Superintendent of Public Instruction of the State of Washington to prepare elementary and secondary education teachers and recommend for certification. It is a member of the American Association of Colleges for Teacher Education. Northwest University's doctoral program in counseling psychology is accredited by the American Psychological Association (APA) . The University is approved by the Federal and State Governments for student aid programs and for the training of international students. Selected programs of study are approved by a Washington State Approving Agency for enrollment of those eligible for benefits under Title 38 and Title 10, U.S. Code and by Washington State for training in Vocational Rehabilitation. It is listed in the current bulletin, \"Accredited Higher Education Institutions,\" published by the U.S. Office of Education. Back to Job Opportunities How Can We Best Serve You? Find Your Major Schedule a Visit Apply Today Address 5520 108th Ave. N.E. Kirkland, WA 98033 Directions Contact 425-822-8266 info@northwestu.edu Campus Map Connect NU Calendar Employment Consumer Information Title IX Emergency Accreditation Finances Social Media Policy Privacy Policy Pay My Bill Northwest University admits students of any race, color, national and ethnic origin to all the rights, privileges, programs, and activities generally afforded or made available to students at the university. Northwest does not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, national and ethnic origin, age, disability, or status as a veteran in the administration of its educational policies, admissions policies, or scholarship and loan programs and athletic and other school-administered programs. © Copyright 2026"
