    "https://www.northwestu.edu/jobs/faculty/nursing-simulation-educator": {
      "title": "Instructor",
      "description": "Instructor - Nursing Simulation (Adjunct) | Northwest University Skip Navigation Menu Close Visit Apply Request Info Give Search Search Admissions + Campus Admission (Undergrad) Online Admission Graduate Admission Northwest Partnership Program International Students College in High School Re-admit or Change Campus Campus Visits and Info Sessions Academics + College of Arts, Sciences, and Technology College of Ministry College of Social and Behavioral Sciences School of Business School of Education School of Nursing School of PA Medicine Center for Leadership Studies Creatio Center for Technology, Media, and Design Faculty Directory Financial Aid + Scholarships Undergraduate Graduate Online Undergraduate Online Graduate Northwest Partnership Program Veterans/Tuition Assistance Glossary of Terms Cost Information Campus Life + NU Calendar Campus Tour Campus Ministries Eagle Store NU Library Student Housing NU Blog About + Mission, Vision, Values Office of the President Upcoming Events Student Consumer Information Student Success Conference and Event Services Job Opportunities Nondiscrimination & Title IX Contact Us Athletics Links For New Students Current Students Parents & Families Alumni Donors Veterans Home Jobs Current Job Opportunities at Northwest Apply Now About NU Explore this Section Job Opportunities On-Campus Student Jobs Part-Time Off Campus Instructor - Nursing Simulation (Adjunct) Position Details Department Buntain School of Nursing Reports To Dean, Buntain School of Nursing Close Date Search procedures will be closed, when a sufficient number of qualified applicants have been identified. Classification Adjunct Faculty, Part-time Position Summary The Buntain School of Nursing is seeking a part-time Simulation Educator for our undergraduate program to provide clinical, educational, and technical expertise of simulation-based activities in the Skills/Simulation Lab. Essential Functions Set-up and teaching simulation sessions. Coordinating and supervising students to ensure that simulation experiences meet course outcomes. Collaborate with nursing faculty and other inter-professional faculty to develop simulation scenarios to promote student learning, critical thinking and clinical decision making. Assisting with faculty development and training related to the use of simulation. Overseeing the collection of evaluation data on learning outcomes for simulation activities and collaborating with faculty to disseminate findings. Qualifications The successful candidate: Holds appropriate degrees from accredited colleges or universities: Masters degree or higher in nursing, or Bachelors degree in nursing with a Master's degree in a related field. Holds a current unrestricted license to practice as a registered nurse in the State of Washington. Has current clinical experience of at least three years. Has a demonstrated record of successful teaching of nursing skills, concepts, and critical thinking. Possesses a deep, personal commitment to Jesus Christ and to the Spirit-filled life. Demonstrates a commitment to the integration of faith and learning. Shows willingness and ability to apply the Christian worldview in simulation design and instruction. Indicates a commitment to helping students to achieve overarching nursing program outcomes and student learning outcomes. Establishes and maintains positive relationships with students, faculty, university staff, clinical site personnel and its clients/patients, and the general constituency of the University. Models best instructional practices in the simulation/skills lab setting. Continually develops professional skills in aspiring students through coaching, modeling, evaluation, feedback, and direct instruction. Compensation Based on highest applicable degree earned, the compensation range per credit is $1,230-1,407 (credit load ranges from 7-10). Application Requirements To be considered as a candidate, the applicant must submit the following documents and information: Letter of interest. Curriculum vitae. Names, addresses, email addresses, and telephone numbers of at least three references. Statement of your understanding of the relationship between the integration of Christian faith and your discipline of study. Brief statement of personal faith journey and church involvements Please email your documents to: Angie Pursley Dean of the Buntain School of Nursing angie.pursley@northwestu.edu Search procedures will be closed, when a sufficient number of qualified applicants have been identified. Applicants are urged to provide sufficient information, so that the application file may be considered complete at the end of the search period. Northwest University Northwest University is a Christian coeducational undergraduate and graduate institution, related to the Assemblies of God, offering baccalaureate and master's, and doctoral level education. The sixty-acre campus is located in Kirkland, Washington, just ten miles from downtown Seattle. The campus is an ideal setting for study, recreation, and inspiration and is centrally located and convenient to industry, business, and commercial activities. Mission Statement We, the people of Northwest University, carry the call of God by continually building a learning community dedicated to spiritual vitality, academic excellence, and empowered engagement with human need. In addition, all faculty members at Northwest University must subscribe to our Statement of Faith . Accreditation Northwest University is accredited by the Northwest Commission on Colleges and Universities (regional). The University is endorsed by the Commission on Christian Higher Education of the Assemblies of God and the Association of Christian Schools International. The University holds membership in the Council of Christian Colleges and Universities . Northwest University's College of Business is accredited by the Accreditation Council for Business Schools and Programs (ACBSP) . The Buntain College of Nursing’s baccalaureate degree is accredited by the Commission on Collegiate Nursing Education . In addition, the College of Nursing has received approval from the Washington State Nursing Care Quality Assurance Commission . The University is also approved by the Board of Education and Superintendent of Public Instruction of the State of Washington to prepare elementary and secondary education teachers and recommend for certification. It is a member of the American Association of Colleges for Teacher Education. Northwest University's doctoral program in counseling psychology is accredited by the American Psychological Association (APA) . The University is approved by the Federal and State Governments for student aid programs and for the training of international students. Selected programs of study are approved by a Washington State Approving Agency for enrollment of those eligible for benefits under Title 38 and Title 10, U.S. Code and by Washington State for training in Vocational Rehabilitation. It is listed in the current bulletin, \"Accredited Higher Education Institutions,\" published by the U.S. Office of Education. Back to Job Opportunities How Can We Best Serve You? Find Your Major Schedule a Visit Apply Today Address 5520 108th Ave. N.E. Kirkland, WA 98033 Directions Contact 425-822-8266 info@northwestu.edu Campus Map Connect NU Calendar Employment Consumer Information Title IX Emergency Accreditation Finances Social Media Policy Privacy Policy Pay My Bill Northwest University admits students of any race, color, national and ethnic origin to all the rights, privileges, programs, and activities generally afforded or made available to students at the university. Northwest does not discriminate on the basis of sex, race, color, national and ethnic origin, age, disability, or status as a veteran in the administration of its educational policies, admissions policies, or scholarship and loan programs and athletic and other school-administered programs. © Copyright 2026"
